The reduced Swift Tesla protocol implementation and public offline vectors are
adapted from Tesla, Inc.'s teslamotors/vehicle-command, pinned to commit:
0a582da430c4aca6d397fb6cbed5b4d6bb380125
https://github.com/teslamotors/vehicle-command
Changes replace Go/generated bindings with a bounded Swift codec and CryptoKit,
and restrict exposed commands to authenticated media reads and explicitly gated
Vehicle Monitor enrollment. Source mapping, changed-file descriptions and the
unmodified upstream Apache-2.0 license are preserved in:
ios/TeslaBLE/PROVENANCE.md
ios/TeslaBLE/LICENSE-TESLA

The optional legacy WebRTC product uses stasel/WebRTC 156.0.0. Its complete
BSD-3-Clause notices, including Google WebRTC attribution, remain in:
ios/App/ThirdPartyNotices.txt

The Node validation harness depends on ws 8.22.0 under MIT; its package retains
the upstream license when installed. No node_modules or Apple SDK binary is
vendored in this source distribution. See THIRD_PARTY.md for all dependencies.

